      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "BOL4 — Love story",
      "content": "Reminding someone of something they already know. Very casual and intimate.\n\nA sugar-rush of a love song, told almost entirely in flashback: the day he handed her a flower, the birthday they snuck out at night, the walk home he kissed her goodbye on, the trip where they traced constellations. It's less a story with a plot than a scrapbook — quick, bright memories stacked on top of each other, held together by the repeated fear that it's all too good to be true.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-잖아**, which means \"you know / isn't it / reminding.\" We'll see how BOL4 uses it in \"Love story.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **알다** — to know\n- **보이다** — to be seen\n- **알잖아** — you know, right?\n- **보이잖아** — you can see it, can't you?\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
